   "notes": "This is not the existing 295 K Vinet record with a reference-subtracted thermal increment. Datchi et al. explicitly define Pth(V,T)=0 at 0 K and Table V supplies a distinct 0 K cold Vinet curve. Peritheos therefore uses thermal_pressure_reference=absolute_zero while keeping Tr=295 K only as the public default temperature and for reference-relative diagnostics. At the printed Table IV lattice parameters, the published coefficients give a 0.584 GPa pressure RMSE, reproducing the paper's stated 0.6 GPa. A q-only unweighted pressure-residual refit gives q=7.35(1.89); the discrepancy from 4(1.5) is less than two combined standard deviations and is plausibly affected by rounded P/a rows and the unpublished regression weights. Section IV's gamma_th0=1.04(1) conflicts with final Table V's 1.04(2); this record follows the final parameter table. The source states that parenthetical errors are fit standard deviations, not absolute uncertainties; pressure-scale uncertainty dominates and coefficient covariance is not published.",
